# Project
Zefflow - An agentic ruby-on-rails backend analyst for health, insights and observability.

# Instructions
- Find project description and workflow rules in `.agents/GENERAL.md`
  - Always refer back to this file - it is your main source of guidance.

# Skills
- Find various skills in the `.agents/skills/` directory
  - The `GENERAL.md` will guide you with the skills.
  - `.agents/skills/` is a nested directory with sub-dirs grouping similar skills together.

# Workflow
1. Make sure you have the context from the `GENERAL.md` in your head before making changes.
2. Determine if any of the skills are needed for the task - load them in if so.
3. Always use the `./notes` as a scratchpad directory
  - Always make short and concise notes to yourself or future agents
  - Expecially important when making desicions or contradicting anything in other notes / `GENERAL.md`
  - Also use this directory for notes to communicate with the developer
    - Mermaid diagrams will be super valuable when sensible.
